// Title: Unusual File Modification by dns.exe
// Sigma ID: 9f383dc0-fdeb-4d56-acbc-9f9f4f8f20f3
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch (Nextron Systems), Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, T1133
// Description: Detects an unexpected file being modified by dns.exe which my indicate activity related to
//   remote code execution or other forms of exploitation as seen in CVE-2020-1350 (SigRed)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/unusual-file-modification-by-dns-exe.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_change/file_change_win_unusual_modification_by_dns_exe.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dns.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\dns.log"))
